  "id": "kanak_ae_ae_pilou",
  "name": "Ae-ae and pilou (Kanak customary dance-song)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Customary dance music of the Kanak of New Caledonia's Grande Terre, documented by Raymond Ammann in Kanak Dance and Music (1997, with CD): men's dance songs such as the ae-ae, sung by small groups for the pilou and other collective dances, accompanied by bark clappers (bwanjep) and bamboo stamping tubes struck on the ground. The cupped hand-clap card stands in for the bark clappers and the stamping-tube card for the Kanak bamboo tubes.",
  "recipe": "classic late-1990s ae-ae and pilou, praise Song, oceania pacific branch. group vocals. cupped muffled hand clap, tagunggak. field recording. ORTF stereo pair, portable field-recorder pre. 24-bit digital.",
